  "reason": "All three Original Updates are executable, grounded in the supplied runs, and compatible with the unchanged Goal, so they are kept without textual change. The current batch strongly supports the search requirement in u2: P3 revisits drawers 1-4 after they were already opened at P3:2-P3:6 (P3:8-P3:11), P6 reopens drawer 1 and drawer 2 repeatedly (P6:6, P6:10, P6:16) and never inspects any of the listed cabinets, and P8 cycles cabinet 1 -> cabinet 2 -> cabinet 3 -> cabinet 4 -> sinkbasin 1 many times (P8:14-P8:16 and onward) without ever inspecting shelf 1, toilet 1, or bathtubbasin 1; P10 only reaches the exact apple after broad cycling and finds it on the diningtable at P10:32, which is consistent with u2's call to broaden to unexamined receptacle types and open surfaces. The exact-target requirement in u1 is directly mirrored by the current P7 counterexample, where the requested butterknife is never seen and the Actor takes and cleans knife 1 (P7:5, P7:7) and moves it to the drawer (P7:9) before hitting the step limit; this is a genuine near-miss substitution, so the requirement is still necessary rather than falsified. The admissibility requirement in u3 is confirmed by P1:4, P6:20, and P8:5, each of which issued a command absent from the current admissible list and received 'Nothing happens', while the direct 'open' action was used successfully at P8:6. Attribution limits: P7 substitutes even though the Parent already contains an equivalent no-substitute clause, so the effectiveness of restating it is unverified and the clause is retained only because it is the correct necessary condition and no executable better formulation is available; likewise the Parent's anti-revisit wording did not prevent cycling, so u2's benefit is a hypothesis, not a proven causal law. The successful desklamp co-location in P1 (bowl carried to dresser 1, use desklamp 1 at P1:9) and the successful exact-target acquisition/conditioning/placement in P10 (take apple 1 at P10:33, cool at P10:35, move to microwave at P10:38) are untouched, preserving demonstrated behavior; the Plan's omission of separate temperature and multi-instance guidance is not a blocker because P10 completed its cooling task without it and no multi-instance task appears in the supplied runs. No new evidence or structural regrouping is required.",
